    "reasoning": "Every field has its own captured worked solution supporting the selected answer. q-78577: direct multiplication gives Z²=Z, hence Z⁵=Z. q-36302: direct multiplication gives C²=C (in particular, its second-row third entry is 6−6−6=−6), hence C³=C. q-6730: dy/dx=(2t)/(3t²+2t); at t=2 this is 4/16=1/4. q-20512: eliminating the first column produces rows (0,1,0|4) and (0,0,−2|8), so y=4, z=−4, and x=5. q-73397: elimination produces rows (0,0,2|2) and (0,−3,−2|7); swapping and normalizing gives the selected echelon matrix. q-8856: the coefficient determinant is 40, and the stated inverse product evaluates to (−1/2,3/4), satisfying both equations. q-102807: the stated inverse product evaluates to (−11,−4), satisfying both equations. In these two inverse-matrix questions, the source uses x to denote the solution vector, although x also names its first scalar component; the choices are correct under that intended vector notation. q-83867 and q-84092: expectation preserves constants. q-84103: 3(−1/6)=−1/2. q-109221: E[X]=0.15+0.30+0.30+1=1.75, so E[−2X]=−3.5. q-109235: −2(−5/2)−4=1. q-109229: 2(10)−3=17. q-131030: linear homogeneous superposition gives 2/x+√x=(2+x√x)/x. q-127033: the coefficients of t form the direction vector (7,5,−5). q-127048: Q−P=(4,5,−4), giving the selected parametrization, which reaches P at t=0 and Q at t=1. These confirmations rely on captured worked solutions, not inferred grading or uncaptured answer keys.",
